RepoMemory sections consulted: core.architecture, core.where_to_edit, core.invariants, core.testing, core.gotchas, core.dependencies
Recon: profiled immutable metric mechanics, all seed splits, temporal anchors, user overlap, recent-history distributions, graph degrees, channel cutoff counts, package versions, and accelerator availability.
Recon discrepancy: availability has zero legal edges by T because every created_at is after 2024-01-01; it will be excluded from temporal sampling.
Implemented: projected cutoff-safe event indexes, all immutable structural mappings, two-layer 96-channel temporal heterogeneous GraphSAGE, held-out link and next-event auxiliary objectives, temporal negative sampling, direct neural churn head, blend/fusion gates, and separate A/B encoder/head chains.
Implemented fallback: 208-feature compact hazard LightGBM with recency, counts, values, gaps, tenure, active-day/session density, diversity, cross-channel activity, and explicit shared-entity degree/decay statistics.
Selection: five training-only forward anchors rejected direct GraphSAGE and embedding fusion; direct mean AUC 0.803090 and fusion 0.887502 versus compact hazard 0.890150, with graph blend weight 0.0.
Feature widening: session/lifetime-gap features improved 4/5 anchors by +0.000525 mean (SE 0.000219); temporal shared-entity statistics improved 5/5 by +0.000610 mean (SE 0.000103) and were retained.
Rejected: Chain-A monthly synthetic landmarks reduced five-anchor mean AUC by 0.000392 and were not used; Chain B retains 204,328 recent synthetic landmarks with outcome windows ending by T.
Debug: complete 20,000-seed pipeline finished in 49.3 seconds and both prediction files passed the local contract checker.
Difficulty resolved: Numba rejected np.searchsorted with a dynamic unicode side argument; integer cutoff boundaries replaced the dynamic side while preserving strict/inclusive semantics.
Difficulty resolved: 13 validation-eligible ratings have null beer_id and were initially dropped from hazard counts; event indexing was split so they remain personal events but are excluded only from entity graph edges.
Post-evaluation internal selection: 300 LightGBM trees improved five-anchor mean AUC by +0.000240 (SE 0.000049) under the comparison seed and +0.000194 (SE 0.000082) under the production seed, so it replaced 600 trees as the simpler regularized setting.
Post-evaluation rejections: repeated-landmark weights, personal conditional gap survival, comment-length/language trends, platform activity normalization, and recent entity-popularity trajectories all failed the training-only forward stability gate and were excluded.
Relational widening retained: top-20 beer-style and six brewer-continent shares over legal 90/365-day histories improved five-anchor mean AUC by +0.000488 (SE 0.000198), with 4/5 anchors positive; the production matrix now has 258 features.
Additional rejection: distinct active-day/session recencies and burst sizes were a tie (+0.000003 mean, 2/5 anchors positive) and were excluded.
Debug after composition widening: complete two-chain run finished in 41.5 seconds with exact prediction shapes and fallback selected.
